        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(workspaces): guard layout JSON.parse against malformed input",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`openclaw workspaces layout set --file <path>` calls `JSON.parse` directly on the file content. If the file contains malformed JSON, the command crashes with a raw `SyntaxError` that lacks file-path context and is confusing for users.\n\nFollows the same pattern as krissding's #109721 — `fix(cli): guard secrets plan JSON.parse against malformed input`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA raw `SyntaxError: Unexpected token ... at position N` gives no indication of which file caused the error or that the problem is malformed JSON. Wrapping in try-catch allows the error to include the file path and a clear message.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBefore: `SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'h', \"this is not\"... is not valid JSON`\nAfter: `Error: Malformed JSON in workspace layout file: /path/to/layout.json — Unexpected token 'h', \"this is not\"...`\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real CLI proof\n\n```\n$ node scripts/proofs/workspaces-json-parse-guard-proof.mjs\n=== PR #109747: guard layout JSON.parse against malformed input ===\n\n── BEFORE (no try-catch around JSON.parse) ──\n  \"trailing comma\": SyntaxError: Expected double-quoted property name in JSON ...\n  \"unclosed brace\": SyntaxError: Expected ',' or '}' after property value in JSON ...\n  \"bare text\":      SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'h', \"this is not\"... is not valid JSON\n  \"empty file\":     SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input\n  ❌ Raw errors — no file path, no context\n\n── AFTER (try-catch + user-friendly error with file path) ──\n  \"trailing comma\": Malformed JSON in workspace layout file: /tmp/...json — Expected ...\n  \"unclosed brace\": Malformed JSON in workspace layout file: /tmp/...json — Expected ...\n  \"bare text\":      Malformed JSON in workspace layout file: /tmp/...json — Unexpected token ...\n  \"empty file\":     Malformed JSON in workspace layout file: /tmp/...json — Unexpected end of JSON input\n  ✅ File path + reason included — user can fix the file\n```\n\nThe proof creates 4 types of malformed JSON files (trailing comma, unclosed brace, bare text, empty) and demonstrates the before/after error messages for each.\n\n### Unit test\n\nNew test (\"shows a user-friendly error when the layout file is malformed JSON\") in `cli.test.ts` verifies the error includes `Malformed JSON` and the file path.",
